<pipeline>
  <info>
    <name>0030-xml-join-chained</name>
    <name_sync_with_filename>Y</name_sync_with_filename>
    <description>Issue #9515: one export document built by a chain of XML Joins. Every join reads the document the join before it wrote, and the last row carries the result of every join. The unit test compares the 'result' row with a golden data set.</description>
    <extended_description/>
    <pipeline_version/>
    <parameters>
    </parameters>
    <capture_transform_performance>N</capture_transform_performance>
    <transform_performance_capturing_delay>1000</transform_performance_capturing_delay>
    <transform_performance_capturing_size_limit>100</transform_performance_capturing_size_limit>
    <created_user>-</created_user>
    <created_date>2026/11/17 12:00:00.000</created_date>
    <modified_user>-</modified_user>
    <modified_date>2026/11/17 12:00:00.000</modified_date>
  </info>
  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <backgroundcolorblue>251</backgroundcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>232</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorred>201</backgroundcolorred>
      <bordercolorblue>90</bordercolorblue>
      <bordercolorgreen>58</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorred>14</bordercolorred>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontcolorblue>90</fontcolorblue>
      <fontcolorgreen>58</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorred>14</fontcolorred>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontname/>
      <fontsize>-1</fontsize>
      <height>140</height>
      <xloc>464</xloc>
      <yloc>320</yloc>
      <note>A chain of XML Joins, each one adds to the document the join before it wrote:
1. add customers: under one node, the root has a namespace prefix: /*[name()='shop:export']/customers
2. add customer C4: the source is the output of another XML Join (build customer C4)
3. add orders: by key on an attribute, String key, two orders for C1
4. add lines: by key on a child element, Integer key, also lines for the order of C4
5. add discounts: by key on a prefixed attribute: @*[name()='shop:sku']
6. add shipments: the key field holds the XPath, later rows go under a shipment an earlier row added
7. add note: under one node by position, with the XML header and omit null values (drops the empty orders of C3)
The XPath statements in 1, 3, 4, 7 are the ones a click in the dialog's target document writes.</note>
      <width>760</width>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
